   "prompt": "<p>For the following exercises, use this information: The inner product of two functions <em>f</em> and <em>g</em> over $[a,b]$ is defined by $f(x)\\cdot g(x)=\\langle f,g\\rangle =\\int_a^{b}f\\cdot gdx.$ Two distinct functions <em>f</em> and <em>g</em> are said to be orthogonal if $\\langle f,g\\rangle =0.$</p><p>Show that $\\{\\sin (2x),\\cos (3x)\\}$ are orthogonal over the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi ].$</p>",
