   "prompt": "<p>For the following exercises, use this information: The inner product of two functions <em>f</em> and <em>g</em> over $[a,b]$ is defined by $f(x)\\cdot g(x)=\\langle f,g\\rangle =\\int_a^{b}f\\cdot gdx.$ Two distinct functions <em>f</em> and <em>g</em> are said to be orthogonal if $\\langle f,g\\rangle =0.$</p><p>Integrate $y^{\\prime}=\\sqrt{\\tan x}{\\sec }^{4}x.$</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "open",
